  Frozen labels: E sqrt(Lambda_n) tends to 1 - Hel(nu(.|x0), coin) = 0.9114 > 0, so Lemma 5.1's bound (1 - Hel_mu)^n fails for frozen data with repeats,
  and the lambda-MAP is the coin for every n and every lambda >= 1: Cor 5.7(c) fails in the frozen reading.
  Fresh labels: the per-query likelihood satisfies Lemma 5.1 with equality and pi* is eventually the MAP.
